What:		/sys/class/power_supply/oplus-pencil/ble_mac_addr
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	Linux Power Supply Mailing List <linux-pm@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
		Bluetooth address of the docked pencil as received over the
		wireless charging link, in xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx form. Reads as
		all zeros while no identified pencil is docked (present is 0).
		The address lets userspace pair with and connect to the
		pencil; the charging link itself does not authenticate it.

		Access: Read
		Valid values: Represented as a colon-separated hexadecimal
		MAC address

What:		/sys/class/power_supply/oplus-pencil/pencil_id
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	Linux Power Supply Mailing List <linux-pm@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
		Pencil model identifier byte from the identity packets, or 0
		while no identified pencil is docked.

		Access: Read
		Valid values: 0 - 255

What:		/sys/class/power_supply/oplus-pencil/misplaced
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	Linux Power Supply Mailing List <linux-pm@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
		1 while the transmitter reports that the pencil sits off the
		charging coil, 0 otherwise. A change event is emitted when
		the state changes.

		Access: Read
		Valid values: 0 or 1

What:		/sys/class/power_supply/oplus-pencil/fw_version
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	Linux Power Supply Mailing List <linux-pm@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
		Transmitter firmware version as major.minor, each four
		hexadecimal digits.

		Access: Read
		Valid values: Represented as string
